* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.pdf binary
*.docx binary
*.xlsx binary
*.woff2 binary
# RFC 5545 requires CRLF line endings; the blanket `eol=lf` rule above would
# silently renormalise them to LF on every commit otherwise. It is the one
# file of this shape this repository ever commits.
instance/public-data/agenda-internal.ics binary

# `declarations/boundary.yml` declares this path `regenerated:` -- rewritten in
# full from the commit history by `.github/workflows/derive-decision-register.yml`, in
# every instance including this one. Upstream's rows and a duplicate's rows
# are both correct, entirely different, and rewritten on both sides between
# any two merges, so git sees two sides that changed the same lines and
# raises a conflict whose only correct resolution is "mine". This is that
# resolution, written down. It needs the driver configured once per clone
# (`git config merge.ours.driver true`); without it git falls back to the
# ordinary conflict, which is the state this replaces.
# `tools/tests/declaration/test_boundary.py` refuses a `regenerated:` path
# that is missing this line.
docs/handbook/governance/register.md merge=ours
